@ 10.1.2.4 - Proto-Philippine to Ibanag
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Llamzon, Teodoro A. (1975), “Proto-Philippine Phonology”. Archipel 9(1):29 – 42; and from other changes and information from this document Something happens to final voiceless stops but it isn’t clear in the paper
	ə > a
	*P:[+voice] > r
	*j > ɡ / possible exception in word-initial position?
	*:[+continuant] > r
	z > r / V_V
	*S > ɡ
	r > d / #_ (?)
	{s,c} > t
	{q,h} > ∅
	uj > i
	iw > uj